{
  "abstract": "TxGraffiti Conjecture 2 asserts Z(G) ≤ α(G) + 1 for every connected graph G of maximum degree at most 3 other than K4, where Z is the zero forcing number and α the independence number (recorded by Davila, Brimkov and Pepper, arXiv:2507.17780). Mikko Fischer found a connected 24-vertex counterexample (arXiv:2607.23664). The package certifies that Fischer's graph is connected, has maximum degree 3, zero forcing number at least 11 and independence number at most 9.",
